Project Overview :

Burnout and mental health deterioration have become a silent crisis in the global tech industry, directly impacting employee 
productivity, retention, and organizational performance.

This project analyzes mental health and burnout data of tech employees using Power BI to help stakeholders understand:

-Burnout patterns across job roles and work modes
-Therapy access vs actual usage gap
-The influence of stress, sleep, and work hours on burnout 
-Which segments are at highest risk of attrition
The dashboard provides a comprehensive view of workforce mental health to support data-driven HR and leadership decisions.
---
Business Problem :
Organizations in the tech industry are investing in remote work, competitive salaries, and mental health benefits — 
yet burnout continues to rise in 2026.

The core challenge is that companies lack clear insights into:

-Which job roles and work modes have the highest burnout risk
-Why employees with therapy access still don't use it
-How burnout directly connects to attrition and financial loss
-Which behavioral and clinical signals indicate a high-risk employee

Without these insights:

-Mental health resources are misallocated
-High-risk employees go unidentified until they resign
-Attrition costs remain invisible to leadership
-Interventions remain generic instead of targeted
---
Stakeholder Expectations :

Different stakeholders expect different insights from the dashboard:
1. Executives (CEO / CHRO)
They want:

-Overall burnout severity across the workforce
-Attrition risk and financial impact
-High-level overview of mental health trends

2. HR & People Teams
They want:
-Which roles and departments need intervention first
-Therapy access and utilization gap analysis
-Demographic breakdown of burnout patterns

3. Mental Health Researchers
They want:
-Clinical score analysis (PHQ-9 and GAD-7)
-Behavioral correlations — sleep, stress, hours worked
-Evidence-based patterns across geographies

---
Project Objectives :

The objective of this project is to build an interactive Power BI dashboard that helps organizations:

-Track burnout severity across 100,000 tech employees
-Analyze the therapy access gap — who has it vs who uses it
-Understand the impact of work mode on mental health outcomes
-Connect burnout data directly to job change intention and attrition risk
-Support targeted, data-backed mental health interventions
